within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.J_AntiinfectivesForSystemicUse.J01A_Tetracyclines.J01AA02_Doxycycline;
model Doxycycline "Doxycycline — default model: Doxycycline_Thompson2019_reference"
  extends Doxycycline_Thompson2019_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of doxycycline: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.J_AntiinfectivesForSystemicUse.J01A_Tetracyclines.J01AA02_Doxycycline.Doxycycline_Thompson2019_reference\">Doxycycline_Thompson2019_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of doxycycline in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Doxycycline_Thompson2019_reference</code></li><li><code>Doxycycline_Zhang2016_PD_kill_rate</code></li></ul><h4>About doxycycline</h4><p>Doxycycline is a tetracycline antibiotic used to treat many bacterial infections, including pneumonia, acne, Lyme disease, and chlamydia, and to prevent malaria. It is widely used in human medicine and is also approved for veterinary use, and it appears on the WHO list of essential medicines.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422442\">Wikidata Q422442</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Doxycycline\">Doxycycline</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>10/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 432000, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Doxycycline;
